A PRODUCT SOURCE THAT REACHES THE HOST PLATFORM'S REGULAR-EXPRESSION ENGINE, so rule N18's
rejecting direction is decided by an input rather than by a comment. It is written the way the
regression would actually arrive: not as somebody replacing the matcher, but as one String method
reaching for the nearest tool, which is how the dialect got in the first time.

It writes all three spellings the rule knows, because a rule that caught only the one a reader
thought of first would report this file and miss the next one.

```csharp
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;

namespace Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript;

internal sealed partial class JsRealm
{
    private static bool LooksLikeAnIdentifier(string text) =>
        new Regex("^[A-Za-z_$][A-Za-z0-9_$]*$").IsMatch(text);

    private static bool LooksLikeANumber(string text) =>
        System.Text.RegularExpressions.Regex.IsMatch(text, "^-?[0-9]+$");
}
```

This file is a witness and is never compiled. It lives here rather than in a product project for
the reason every rejecting witness does: a file that would make the rule fail cannot live where the
rule looks.
